From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] GS CPU backend: optional row bands, to draw one picture on several threads

What broke:
  Nothing is wrong, but slow: the CPU rasteriser draws every pixel of the
  frame on one thread. Ben 10: Protector of Earth's port runs it on a
  thread of its own (src/gs/gs_async_backend.cpp, through the public
  GS::setRasterBackend), where it is busy nearly all the time in the
  first level (39 of 40 gdb samples, findings/20 s.6).

The fix:
  GSCpuBackend::SetRowBand(index, count): with count > 1 the backend draws
  only the rows y with ((y >> 4) % count) == index (triangle and sprite
  row loops skip the other rows; WritePixel checks too, for lines and
  points). Default count = 1: unchanged behaviour. Several backends that
  share GS memory and receive the same primitives, CLUT loads and
  TEXFLUSHes in the same order then write exactly the bytes one backend
  writes, each pixel being drawn by one band; the caller must not let a
  band read a page (texture, CLUT) another band has not finished writing.
  Tested: new ps2xTest case "GS CPU backends drawing row bands of one
  picture write the same bytes as one backend" (blended Gouraud
  triangles, Z test, a textured blended sprite; two bands drawn one after
  the other, the worst order) compares the frame and Z buffers with one
  backend: identical. 452/452 ps2xTest cases pass.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/gs/gs_cpu_backend.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/gs/gs_cpu_backend.h
@@ -33,7 +33,24 @@
     void SnapshotVram(std::vector<uint8_t> &out) const override;
     GSTransferSnapshot GetTransferSnapshot() const override;
 
+    // Row bands, for drawing one picture with several backends at once:
+    // with count > 1 this backend draws only the pixels of rows y where
+    // ((y >> kRowBandShift) % count) == index, and skips the others. Each
+    // pixel belongs to exactly one band, so backends that share GS memory
+    // and see the same primitives in the same order write the same bytes as
+    // one backend. count <= 1 (the default) draws every row.
+    static constexpr uint32_t kRowBandShift = 4u;
+    void SetRowBand(uint32_t index, uint32_t count);
+
 private:
+    bool rowInBand(int y) const noexcept
+    {
+        return m_rowBandCount <= 1u ||
+               ((static_cast<uint32_t>(y) >> kRowBandShift) % m_rowBandCount) == m_rowBandIndex;
+    }
+    uint32_t m_rowBandIndex = 0u;
+    uint32_t m_rowBandCount = 1u;
+
     void ResetUnlocked();
     void LoadClutUnlocked(const GSTex0Reg &tex0, const GSTexClutReg &texclut);
     uint32_t ReadVramUnlocked(uint32_t psm, uint32_t base, uint32_t bw, uint32_t x, uint32_t y) const;
